WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.670
Choose any four different whole numbers.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.500
Prove that two of them always have a difference that is

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.550
a multiple of three.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.150
You can choose very large numbers if you like.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.190
How can one argument cover every possible choice?

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.760
Divide a whole number by three.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.300
The remainder can be zero, one or two.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.420
A leftover of three would make another complete group.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.810
Create one box for each of the

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.300
three allowable remainders.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.240
Every chosen number belongs to exactly one box.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.830
Four numbers and three boxes force at least two numbers

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.980
into the same box.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.380
Those two numbers have the same remainder.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.610
We can use that single fact to show their difference is

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.740
a multiple of three.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.150
Write the larger number as three a plus r,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.190
and the smaller as three b plus the same r.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.380
On subtracting, the two r terms cancel.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.290
The result is three times the difference between

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.220
a and b.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.640
It is a whole number of groups of three.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.000
Try two, six, ten and thirteen.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.100
Ten and thirteen both leave remainder one.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.620
Their difference is three.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.040
Could three numbers guarantee the result?

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.800
With one, two and three, the remainders all differ.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.860
Their differences are one or two.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.410
This shows four is the smallest number that

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.360
guarantees a match.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.330
Choose a box for each remainder and use subtraction once

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.780
two numbers share a box.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.340
Now increase the divisor to ten.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.370
How many different whole numbers guarantee that two

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.040
differ by a multiple of ten?

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.250
Show both why your answer works and how one fewer

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.280
choice could fail.
